+---
+id: task-004-implement-json-merge-patch-rfc-7386-applymergepatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386) applyMergePatch"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Some clients send partial updates in the simpler JSON Merge Patch format. Implement JSON Merge Patch,
+as specified in RFC 7386: export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`, which applies a
+merge patch to a target JSON document and returns the merged document.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Design recorded in dl-004-json-merge-patch-api-json-values-only-copy-on-apply-jsonmergepatcherror.
+- `test/json-merge-patch.test.ts`: 13 tests written first (all red: the export did not exist): every
+  example of RFC 7386 appendix A and section 3, removal of a missing member, non-object targets, nulls
+  inside arrays, falsy values, no mutation, no shared objects, `__proto__` and inherited members,
+  non-JSON targets and patches, null-prototype objects and shared sub-values.
+- `src/index.ts`: `JsonMergePatchError` and `applyMergePatch`, reusing the JSON-value helpers of
+  `applyPatch`.
+- `README.md`: a JSON Merge Patch section.
+- `npm test`: 65 tests pass. `tsc` is not installed here, so the type check was not run.
